# Liquid Glass design rules (v2.0.0)

## Core principles
- Glass belongs ONLY to the navigation/chrome layer; NEVER on content (articles, feeds, table cells)
- NEVER stack glass on glass; controls inside glass use flat fills (`.glass-btn--plain`, `var(--glass-fill)`)
- Glass needs a backdrop worth seeing through (photos, video, wallpapers, scrolling content)
- Concentric radii: inner radius = outer radius minus padding

## Base glass surface CSS
```css
.glass-surface {
  position: relative;
  isolation: isolate;
  border-radius: 26px;
  background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.08);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(8px) saturate(180%);
  backdrop-filter: blur(8px) saturate(180%);
  box-shadow:
    inset 1.5px 1.5px 0 -0.5px rgb(255 255 255 / 0.6),
    inset -1px -1px 0 -0.5px rgb(255 255 255 / 0.4),
    inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1),
    0 10px 28px -10px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.45);
  outline: 1px solid transparent;
  color: #fff;
}
```
Prefer the tokens in `tokens.css` (`var(--glass-bg)`, `var(--glass-shadow-rim)`) over these literals.

## Refraction
- Add `data-refract` and load `liquid-glass.js` for real refraction (Chromium desktop only)
- Every component must look complete without it; never use a 20px+ blur to compensate

## Interaction
- Pressed controls grow (`scale: var(--glass-press-scale)`), never shrink
- Switch and slider thumbs become a clear lens while held (`:active`)
- Selections slide between items; springs use `linear()` over 600ms

## Mandatory fallbacks (include ALL)
- `prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce`: solid bg, `backdrop-filter: none !important`
- `prefers-contrast: more`: solid bg, 2px outline, no shadows
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`: no transitions
- `forced-colors: active`: Canvas/CanvasText system colours

## Typography: weight 500+, 16px body. No mix-blend-mode on text.
## Performance: at most 3 glass surfaces on mobile. No will-change: backdrop-filter.

See `skills/liquid-glass/SKILL.md` and `snippets/tokens.css` for the full system.
